; expect 42
; `Mod::name` disambiguates when several modules export the same name,
; and it is how B4's qualified access is spelled. stage1 could not
; parse it at all: `parseIdentRef` committed to a field-access chain as
; each `.` was consumed, so the `::` was never reached.
;
; A qualified reference needs no node of its own. The module path
; joined by `.`, then `$`, then the name IS the mangled symbol every
; imported declaration already carries - `Mem::memAlloc` is
; `Mem$memAlloc`, exactly what `mangleDecl` wrote - so it resolves to
; an ordinary variable reference and the checker and emitter need to
; know nothing about it.
(import Mem)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (if (>
    (Mem::memAlloc
      64
    )    0
  )
    42
    1
  )
)
